steps {
  type: CORTEX_STEP_TYPE_USER_INPUT
  status: CORTEX_STEP_STATUS_DONE
  metadata {
    created_at {
      seconds: 1786641652
      nanos: 140830601
    }
    source: CORTEX_STEP_SOURCE_USER_EXPLICIT
  }
  user_input {
    user_response: "## Project: CraftDocs \342\200\224 A Minecraft-Themed Document Editor\n\nBuild a fully functional, single-page web application called **CraftDocs** using **React + TypeScript + Vite**. Use **Tailwind CSS** for styling. Do NOT use any external rich-text editor libraries (no Quill, no TipTap, no Slate) \342\200\224 build the editor logic from scratch using `contenteditable` and the browser Selection API to demonstrate engineering depth.\n\n---\n\n### Core Concept\n\nCraftDocs is a document editor that blends Google Docs and Notion, wrapped entirely in a **Minecraft pixel-art UI theme**. The key innovation is a **mode switch** \342\200\224 users toggle between two editing philosophies using a button in the top bar:\n\n- \342\232\224\357\270\217 **Survival Mode** = Google Docs style (linear document, WYSIWYG, continuous text flow, formatting toolbar)\n- \360\237\247\261 **Creative Mode** = Notion style (block-based, each paragraph/heading/image is a draggable block, slash `/` command menu to insert new block types)\n\nWhen the user switches modes, the same document content re-renders in the other paradigm \342\200\224 content is never lost.\n\n---\n\n### Minecraft UI Theme \342\200\224 Apply Everywhere, No Exceptions\n\nEvery single UI element must look like it belongs inside Minecraft. This is not optional. Specific requirements:\n\n**Fonts:**\n- Import and use the `\"Press Start 2P\"` Google Font (pixel/8-bit style) for all headings, labels, toolbar buttons, and UI chrome.\n- The document body text (what the user types) should use a readable monospace or serif font like `\"Courier New\"` or `\"Georgia\"` so it stays legible.\n\n**Top Toolbar (the Hotbar):**\n- Style it exactly like Minecraft\'s **hotbar** \342\200\224 a dark stone-textured horizontal bar across the top.\n- Use CSS to create a `repeating-linear-gradient` or `background-image` pattern that mimics the **stone/cobblestone block texture** (dark gray, #3f3f3f, with subtle pixel-grid noise).\n- Each toolbar button (Bold, Italic, Heading, etc.) sits inside a **square inventory slot** \342\200\224 48\303\22748px, dark grey background (#2d2d2d), inset box-shadow to look pressed, 2px solid #555 border. On hover, glow with a golden outline (#FFD700).\n- Use pixel-art emoji or Unicode symbols as button icons: \342\232\224\357\270\217 Bold, \360\237\223\234 Italic, \360\237\252\250 Heading 1, \360\237\247\261 Heading 2, \360\237\223\213 List, \360\237\222\216 Link, \360\237\227\272\357\270\217 Image.\n- The active/selected button has a golden border and a subtle yellow background highlight.\n\n**Mode Switch Button:**\n- A large toggle button in the top-right of the hotbar, styled like a **Minecraft enchanted item** (purple shimmer animation using CSS keyframes when in Creative Mode, normal stone look in Survival Mode).\n- Shows: `\342\232\224\357\270\217 SURVIVAL` or `\360\237\247\261 CREATIVE` in Press Start 2P font.\n\n**Sidebar (Notion-style page tree \342\200\224 always visible):**\n- Background: **Dark Oak Wood plank texture** \342\200\224 `repeating-linear-gradient` of alternating #3b2a1a and #2e2012, horizontal stripes, 4px each.\n- Title: \"\360\237\223\232 INVENTORY\" in Press Start 2P, gold color.\n- Each page entry looks like an **inventory item row** \342\200\224 icon (\360\237\223\204), page name, indented child pages. Hover shows a stone-style highlight.\n- A `+ NEW PAGE` button styled like a **crafting table output slot** \342\200\224 green border, animated pulse.\n\n**Document Canvas:**\n- Background: **Parchment/Book texture** \342\200\224 a warm off-white (`#fdf6e3`) with a very subtle `noise` CSS filter or repeating dot pattern to simulate aged paper, like the in-game Book & Quill.\n- A thin pixel-border (4px, brown `#8B6914`) wraps the entire editor area.\n- The blinking text cursor should be a **blocky 2px-wide rectangle cursor** (achieved via CSS caret-colour and custom styling).\n\n**Slash Command Menu (Creative Mode):**\n- A floating panel styled like the **Minecraft chat/inventory window** \342\200\224 dark (#1a1a2e) background, 2px stone border, slight transparency.\n- Each command option (Text, Heading 1, Heading 2, Bullet List, Numbered List, Divider, Quote, Code Block, Image) is a row with a pixel-art icon and name in Press Start 2P (small size).\n- Highlight on hover with a blue Minecraft-selection blue (#3a5fcd).\n\n**Status Bar (Bottom):**\n- Full-width bar at the bottom, styled as a **Minecraft XP bar**.\n- Left side: green XP-bar fill that represents `word count / 1000` words (max fill at 1000+ words). Shows \"\342\254\233 [====    ] 247 WORDS\" in pixel font.\n- Right side: show mode, last saved time (\"\360\237\222\276 SAVED\"), and a small creeper face emoji.\n\n**Notifications/Toasts:**\n- When the user does something notable (saves, switches mode, creates a page), show a **Minecraft Achievement popup** in the top-right: dark background, golden border, achievement icon, and text like \"Achievement Unlocked: First Document!\" in Press Start 2P.\n\n---\n\n### Features to Implement\n\n**Survival Mode (Google Docs):**\n- Formatting: Bold (`Ctrl+B`), Italic (`Ctrl+I`), Underline (`Ctrl+U`) via `document.execCommand` or Selection API.\n- Heading styles: H1, H2, H3 applied to the selected line.\n- Bullet list and numbered list.\n- Undo/Redo via `Ctrl+Z` / `Ctrl+Y`.\n- Word count shown in status bar (live, updates on every keystroke).\n- Auto-save to `localStorage` every 30 seconds \342\200\224 show \"\360\237\222\276 SAVING...\" then \"\360\237\222\276 SAVED\" in the status bar.\n\n**Creative Mode (Notion Blocks):**\n- The document is rendered as a vertical stack of **Block** components.\n- Each block has a type: `text | heading1 | heading2 | heading3 | bulletList | numberedList | quote | code | divider | image`.\n- Pressing `Enter` at the end of a block creates a new empty `text` block below.\n- Pressing `/` at the start of an empty block opens the **Slash Command Menu** \342\200\224 typing filters the options, pressing `Enter` or clicking selects a block type.\n- Each block has a **drag handle** (\342\213\256\342\213\256 icon, appears on hover on the left) \342\200\224 blocks are reorderable via drag-and-drop (implement with `HTML5 Drag and Drop API`, not a library).\n- Clicking a block selects it. A selected block shows inline formatting options in a small floating toolbar above it (Bold, Italic, Link).\n- Pressing `Backspace` on an empty block deletes it and focuses the previous block.\n\n**Page Management (Sidebar):**\n- Users can create multiple pages, each with its own title and content.\n- Pages are stored in `localStorage` as a JSON tree structure.\n- Pages can be nested (drag a page onto another to make it a child \342\200\224 show indentation).\n- Clicking a page loads it into the editor.\n- Double-click a page name to rename it inline.\n- Right-click a page to show a context menu: Rename, Duplicate, Delete \342\200\224 styled as a Minecraft inventory action menu.\n\n---\n\n### Data Model (TypeScript interfaces \342\200\224 define these)\n\n```typescript\ninterface Block {\n  id: string;\n  type: \'text\' | \'heading1\' | \'heading2\' | \'heading3\' | \'bulletList\' | \'numberedList\' | \'quote\' | \'code\' | \'divider\' | \'image\';\n  content: string;\n  children?: Block[];\n}\n\ninterface Page {\n  id: string;\n  title: string;\n  blocks: Block[];\n  children: Page[];\n  createdAt: number;\n  updatedAt: number;\n}\n\ninterface EditorState {\n  pages: Page[];\n  activePage: string | null;\n  mode: \'survival\' | \'creative\';\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### File Structure\n\n```\nsrc/\n  components/\n    Toolbar.tsx          # Top hotbar with formatting buttons\n    Sidebar.tsx          # Page tree / inventory panel\n    StatusBar.tsx        # XP bar at the bottom\n    SurvivalEditor.tsx   # Google Docs-style contenteditable editor\n    CreativeEditor.tsx   # Notion-style block editor\n    Block.tsx            # Single block component for Creative mode\n    SlashMenu.tsx        # Slash command floating menu\n    Toast.tsx            # Achievement popup notifications\n    ModeToggle.tsx       # Survival/Creative switch button\n  hooks/\n    useEditor.ts         # Core editor state and actions\n    useAutoSave.ts       # localStorage auto-save logic\n    useSlashMenu.ts      # Slash menu open/close/filter logic\n  types/\n    editor.ts            # All TypeScript interfaces\n  styles/\n    minecraft.css        # All Minecraft texture CSS (stone, oak, parchment patterns)\n  App.tsx\n  main.tsx\n```\n\n---\n\n### Additional Requirements\n\n- The entire app must be **fully dark-themed** by default (stone/obsidian palette) with the document canvas being the only light area (parchment).\n- All CSS animations must use `@keyframes` \342\200\224 the enchanted-item shimmer onthe  Creative mode toggle, the achievement popup slide-in, the XP bar fill animation.\n- The app must be **fully responsive** down to 768px (tablet). On mobile, the sidebar collapses into a hamburger menu styled as a Minecraft chest icon (\360\237\216\222).\n- Add a `README.md` explaining the architecture: block data model, mode-switching design decision, localStorage persistence strategy.\n- Write clean, typed TypeScript \342\200\224 no `any` types. All components must have typed props interfaces.\n- Code must be well-commented, explaining non-obvious design decisions (especially the Selection API usage in Survival Mode and the drag-and-drop logic in Creative Mode).\n\nGenerate the complete working application. Start with `minecraft.css` and the TypeScript type definitions, then build each component. Finally, provide a clear folder structure for the final project components.\n\nFor the React-based Minecraft clone project structure and file hierarchy.\n\nAfter completing, make a GitHub repo and push everything there"
    items {
      text: "## Project: CraftDocs \342\200\224 A Minecraft-Themed Document Editor\n\nBuild a fully functional, single-page web application called **CraftDocs** using **React + TypeScript + Vite**. Use **Tailwind CSS** for styling. Do NOT use any external rich-text editor libraries (no Quill, no TipTap, no Slate) \342\200\224 build the editor logic from scratch using `contenteditable` and the browser Selection API to demonstrate engineering depth.\n\n---\n\n### Core Concept\n\nCraftDocs is a document editor that blends Google Docs and Notion, wrapped entirely in a **Minecraft pixel-art UI theme**. The key innovation is a **mode switch** \342\200\224 users toggle between two editing philosophies using a button in the top bar:\n\n- \342\232\224\357\270\217 **Survival Mode** = Google Docs style (linear document, WYSIWYG, continuous text flow, formatting toolbar)\n- \360\237\247\261 **Creative Mode** = Notion style (block-based, each paragraph/heading/image is a draggable block, slash `/` command menu to insert new block types)\n\nWhen the user switches modes, the same document content re-renders in the other paradigm \342\200\224 content is never lost.\n\n---\n\n### Minecraft UI Theme \342\200\224 Apply Everywhere, No Exceptions\n\nEvery single UI element must look like it belongs inside Minecraft. This is not optional. Specific requirements:\n\n**Fonts:**\n- Import and use the `\"Press Start 2P\"` Google Font (pixel/8-bit style) for all headings, labels, toolbar buttons, and UI chrome.\n- The document body text (what the user types) should use a readable monospace or serif font like `\"Courier New\"` or `\"Georgia\"` so it stays legible.\n\n**Top Toolbar (the Hotbar):**\n- Style it exactly like Minecraft\'s **hotbar** \342\200\224 a dark stone-textured horizontal bar across the top.\n- Use CSS to create a `repeating-linear-gradient` or `background-image` pattern that mimics the **stone/cobblestone block texture** (dark gray, #3f3f3f, with subtle pixel-grid noise).\n- Each toolbar button (Bold, Italic, Heading, etc.) sits inside a **square inventory slot** \342\200\224 48\303\22748px, dark grey background (#2d2d2d), inset box-shadow to look pressed, 2px solid #555 border. On hover, glow with a golden outline (#FFD700).\n- Use pixel-art emoji or Unicode symbols as button icons: \342\232\224\357\270\217 Bold, \360\237\223\234 Italic, \360\237\252\250 Heading 1, \360\237\247\261 Heading 2, \360\237\223\213 List, \360\237\222\216 Link, \360\237\227\272\357\270\217 Image.\n- The active/selected button has a golden border and a subtle yellow background highlight.\n\n**Mode Switch Button:**\n- A large toggle button in the top-right of the hotbar, styled like a **Minecraft enchanted item** (purple shimmer animation using CSS keyframes when in Creative Mode, normal stone look in Survival Mode).\n- Shows: `\342\232\224\357\270\217 SURVIVAL` or `\360\237\247\261 CREATIVE` in Press Start 2P font.\n\n**Sidebar (Notion-style page tree \342\200\224 always visible):**\n- Background: **Dark Oak Wood plank texture** \342\200\224 `repeating-linear-gradient` of alternating #3b2a1a and #2e2012, horizontal stripes, 4px each.\n- Title: \"\360\237\223\232 INVENTORY\" in Press Start 2P, gold color.\n- Each page entry looks like an **inventory item row** \342\200\224 icon (\360\237\223\204), page name, indented child pages. Hover shows a stone-style highlight.\n- A `+ NEW PAGE` button styled like a **crafting table output slot** \342\200\224 green border, animated pulse.\n\n**Document Canvas:**\n- Background: **Parchment/Book texture** \342\200\224 a warm off-white (`#fdf6e3`) with a very subtle `noise` CSS filter or repeating dot pattern to simulate aged paper, like the in-game Book & Quill.\n- A thin pixel-border (4px, brown `#8B6914`) wraps the entire editor area.\n- The blinking text cursor should be a **blocky 2px-wide rectangle cursor** (achieved via CSS caret-colour and custom styling).\n\n**Slash Command Menu (Creative Mode):**\n- A floating panel styled like the **Minecraft chat/inventory window** \342\200\224 dark (#1a1a2e) background, 2px stone border, slight transparency.\n- Each command option (Text, Heading 1, Heading 2, Bullet List, Numbered List, Divider, Quote, Code Block, Image) is a row with a pixel-art icon and name in Press Start 2P (small size).\n- Highlight on hover with a blue Minecraft-selection blue (#3a5fcd).\n\n**Status Bar (Bottom):**\n- Full-width bar at the bottom, styled as a **Minecraft XP bar**.\n- Left side: green XP-bar fill that represents `word count / 1000` words (max fill at 1000+ words). Shows \"\342\254\233 [====    ] 247 WORDS\" in pixel font.\n- Right side: show mode, last saved time (\"\360\237\222\276 SAVED\"), and a small creeper face emoji.\n\n**Notifications/Toasts:**\n- When the user does something notable (saves, switches mode, creates a page), show a **Minecraft Achievement popup** in the top-right: dark background, golden border, achievement icon, and text like \"Achievement Unlocked: First Document!\" in Press Start 2P.\n\n---\n\n### Features to Implement\n\n**Survival Mode (Google Docs):**\n- Formatting: Bold (`Ctrl+B`), Italic (`Ctrl+I`), Underline (`Ctrl+U`) via `document.execCommand` or Selection API.\n- Heading styles: H1, H2, H3 applied to the selected line.\n- Bullet list and numbered list.\n- Undo/Redo via `Ctrl+Z` / `Ctrl+Y`.\n- Word count shown in status bar (live, updates on every keystroke).\n- Auto-save to `localStorage` every 30 seconds \342\200\224 show \"\360\237\222\276 SAVING...\" then \"\360\237\222\276 SAVED\" in the status bar.\n\n**Creative Mode (Notion Blocks):**\n- The document is rendered as a vertical stack of **Block** components.\n- Each block has a type: `text | heading1 | heading2 | heading3 | bulletList | numberedList | quote | code | divider | image`.\n- Pressing `Enter` at the end of a block creates a new empty `text` block below.\n- Pressing `/` at the start of an empty block opens the **Slash Command Menu** \342\200\224 typing filters the options, pressing `Enter` or clicking selects a block type.\n- Each block has a **drag handle** (\342\213\256\342\213\256 icon, appears on hover on the left) \342\200\224 blocks are reorderable via drag-and-drop (implement with `HTML5 Drag and Drop API`, not a library).\n- Clicking a block selects it. A selected block shows inline formatting options in a small floating toolbar above it (Bold, Italic, Link).\n- Pressing `Backspace` on an empty block deletes it and focuses the previous block.\n\n**Page Management (Sidebar):**\n- Users can create multiple pages, each with its own title and content.\n- Pages are stored in `localStorage` as a JSON tree structure.\n- Pages can be nested (drag a page onto another to make it a child \342\200\224 show indentation).\n- Clicking a page loads it into the editor.\n- Double-click a page name to rename it inline.\n- Right-click a page to show a context menu: Rename, Duplicate, Delete \342\200\224 styled as a Minecraft inventory action menu.\n\n---\n\n### Data Model (TypeScript interfaces \342\200\224 define these)\n\n```typescript\ninterface Block {\n  id: string;\n  type: \'text\' | \'heading1\' | \'heading2\' | \'heading3\' | \'bulletList\' | \'numberedList\' | \'quote\' | \'code\' | \'divider\' | \'image\';\n  content: string;\n  children?: Block[];\n}\n\ninterface Page {\n  id: string;\n  title: string;\n  blocks: Block[];\n  children: Page[];\n  createdAt: number;\n  updatedAt: number;\n}\n\ninterface EditorState {\n  pages: Page[];\n  activePage: string | null;\n  mode: \'survival\' | \'creative\';\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### File Structure\n\n```\nsrc/\n  components/\n    Toolbar.tsx          # Top hotbar with formatting buttons\n    Sidebar.tsx          # Page tree / inventory panel\n    StatusBar.tsx        # XP bar at the bottom\n    SurvivalEditor.tsx   # Google Docs-style contenteditable editor\n    CreativeEditor.tsx   # Notion-style block editor\n    Block.tsx            # Single block component for Creative mode\n    SlashMenu.tsx        # Slash command floating menu\n    Toast.tsx            # Achievement popup notifications\n    ModeToggle.tsx       # Survival/Creative switch button\n  hooks/\n    useEditor.ts         # Core editor state and actions\n    useAutoSave.ts       # localStorage auto-save logic\n    useSlashMenu.ts      # Slash menu open/close/filter logic\n  types/\n    editor.ts            # All TypeScript interfaces\n  styles/\n    minecraft.css        # All Minecraft texture CSS (stone, oak, parchment patterns)\n  App.tsx\n  main.tsx\n```\n\n---\n\n### Additional Requirements\n\n- The entire app must be **fully dark-themed** by default (stone/obsidian palette) with the document canvas being the only light area (parchment).\n- All CSS animations must use `@keyframes` \342\200\224 the enchanted-item shimmer onthe  Creative mode toggle, the achievement popup slide-in, the XP bar fill animation.\n- The app must be **fully responsive** down to 768px (tablet). On mobile, the sidebar collapses into a hamburger menu styled as a Minecraft chest icon (\360\237\216\222).\n- Add a `README.md` explaining the architecture: block data model, mode-switching design decision, localStorage persistence strategy.\n- Write clean, typed TypeScript \342\200\224 no `any` types. All components must have typed props interfaces.\n- Code must be well-commented, explaining non-obvious design decisions (especially the Selection API usage in Survival Mode and the drag-and-drop logic in Creative Mode).\n\nGenerate the complete working application. Start with `minecraft.css` and the TypeScript type definitions, then build each component. Finally, provide a clear folder structure for the final project components.\n\nFor the React-based Minecraft clone project structure and file hierarchy.\n\nAfter completing, make a GitHub repo and push everything there"
    }
  }
}
