  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing the Architecture**\n\nOkay, I\'m starting to build out the architecture as requested. I\'ve begun reviewing the prompt, particularly the structural and feature components. I\'m focusing on the first element, types, specifically `/src/types/editor.ts`, to establish the foundation.\n\n\n**Analyzing Mode Interplay**\n\nI\'m now diving into the interplay between Survival and Creative modes. I\'m focusing on the conversion process. Specifically, when switching to Creative Mode, content is translated from standard HTML (within a continuous `contenteditable` container or converted from `Blocks`) into an array of `Block` objects. I\'m considering the implications for content fidelity and user experience.\n\n\n**Implementing the Conversion**\n\nI\'ve been working on the conversion between `Block` objects and HTML. The focus is now on the converter utility `/src/utils/converter.ts`, which I\'m building out. The main functions are `blocksToHtml(blocks: Block[]): string` and its counterpart. My plan is to correctly translate various HTML elements like headings, lists, quotes, and code into their respective `Block` representations, ensuring a seamless round trip between Creative and Survival modes. I\'m prioritizing accuracy to prevent any content loss during mode switching, as requested.\n\n\n**Defining Block Mapping**\n\nI\'m now deep in defining how we\'ll map HTML elements to our `Block` objects. I\'ve fleshed out the logic for `htmlToBlocks()`. It iterates through HTML elements, converting `H1`, `H2`, `H3`, `UL`, `OL`, `BLOCKQUOTE`, `PRE`, `CODE`, `HR`, `IMG`, `P`, and raw text into their block counterparts. For images, I\'m handling the `src` attribute. I\'ve also identified the need for more test coverage to ensure accuracy. I\'m focusing on handling text content appropriately within these blocks, as well.\n\n\n**Styling Component Visuals**\n\nI\'m now implementing the visual styles for the various UI components. I\'ve focused on creating unique styles for several elements. I\'ve defined the `mc-enchanted` shimmer animation using a linear gradient and keyframes, as requested. The texture for `mc-oak-wood-bg` is a repeating linear gradient. I also implemented `mc-parchment-bg`, including a brown pixel border. The chat window (`mc-chat-window`) uses a dark color palette with a stone border and inset shadow. I\'m actively working on the XP bar (`mc-xp-bar`) using the lime-green color fill, and the achievement style (`mc-achievement`) with dark gray and gold/yellow accents.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 8
      nanos: 6981650
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
