    thinking: "**Constructing Visual Components**\n\nI\'m now diving into the specifics, starting with the `ModeToggle.tsx` component. The current plan is a dynamic button: enchanted shimmer for Creative Mode and a regular stone texture in Survival Mode. This visual distinction should immediately communicate the game mode.\n\n\n**Designing Toolbar Interface**\n\nI\'ve been working on the toolbar, and I\'m envisioning the hotbar with a stone cobblestone background. Each slot will be a square with an inset shadow and a golden outline on hover or active. I\'m also planning out the formatting actions for Survival mode and including undo/redo buttons. The ModeToggle button will sit on the right.\n\n\n**Expanding UI Elements**\n\nMy focus has shifted to integrating a mobile-responsive drawer toggle, marked with a chest icon, `\360\237\216\222`. I\'m also planning the `StatusBar`, emulating the Minecraft XP bar, dynamically filled with green based on word count.  It will also display the mode badge, auto-save status and the Creeper emoji. I\'m imagining Achievement Unlocked-style popups, context menus, slash menus, and draggable block components.\n\n\n**Implementing Editor Modes**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the editor components. Creative mode will use a canvas wrapper to render block components on parchment. Survival mode, in contrast, will employ a Google Docs-style `contenteditable` sheet. I\'m prioritizing the implementation of `ModeToggle.tsx` for visual and functional consistency. I\'m also planning to support HTML5 drag and drop to reorder elements.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 4
      nanos: 648096952
    }
