  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Geometric Balance**\n\nI\'m currently focused on pinpointing the necessary CSS and component styling adjustments to perfectly align the app with the **Geometric Balance** theme. My primary emphasis is ensuring all existing functionality remains untouched during these changes. Right now, I\'m specifically examining the implications of background modifications in the broader design context.\n\n\n**Implementing Visual Styling**\n\nI\'ve established the foundational styling components for the header, hotbar, and sidebar elements. Specifically, I\'ve defined background colors, borders, and text colors. I\'m focusing on applying box-shadow to achieve the desired visual depth. I\'m also ensuring the document canvas and achievement popups match the desired aesthetic. I\342\200\231m currently refining the hover effects to harmonize with the overall design.\n\n\n**Defining Style Attributes**\n\nI\'m currently updating `/src/styles/minecraft.css` with the new style definitions. I\'m focusing on the slash command menu, footer, and XP bar. The slash command menu will have a `bg-[#1a1a2e]` with a `border-2 border-[#3f3f3f]` and `box-shadow`. The footer will have a black top border and items in the center with a defined height. Also, the XP bar track and fill colors. I am examining lines 17-215. The `.mc-stone-bg` and `.mc-slot` styles will have to change.\n\n\n**Refining Slot Interactions**\n\nI\'m focused on the `.mc-slot` styles within `/src/styles/minecraft.css`. I\'ve added hover effects with a gold border and inner box shadow, along with the `active` state with gold highlights and increased outer glow. The box shadow is the key attribute. I\'ve been experimenting with the inset and outer shadows.\n\n\n"
