  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Initiating Character Design**\n\nI\'m now diving into the design of new capabilities and components. First up: the character selection and assistant agent. I\'m focusing on the signup and character selection modal, specifically the initial prompt to select Steve upon app launch or through a dedicated button.\n\n\n**Defining Character Choices**\n\nI\'ve been fleshing out the player character options. The user can select from Steve (classic look) or Alex, or enter a custom username, which gets saved in `localStorage`. Now I\'m focusing on the animated assistant widget. I envision an 8-bit character at the bottom-right, with idle animations.\n\n\n**Adding Explosive Effects**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in sound design and animations, thinking about adding exciting features. I\'m focusing on the \"Spawn Creeper \360\237\222\245\" button, which plays an authentic Minecraft explosion sound sequence and accompanying animations. The animated Creeper pixel sprite walks onto the page, plays a `tsssss...` sound, flashes, and shakes the screen violently. I\'m also planning the scorched bedrock block that replaces the page content.\n\n\n**Implementing Text Formatting**\n\nI\'m now implementing expanded text formatting features within the document editor. This involves integrating text alignment tools, a font family selector with options like Courier Prime and Press Start 2P, and a range of font sizes. I\'m also adding a rich color palette, drawing inspiration from Minecraft dyes, for text coloring and highlighting. Inline code styling and strikethrough features are also in the works.\n\n\n**Expanding Block Features**\n\nI\'m now focused on adding interactive checklist items with pixel checkboxes and strikethrough functionality. I\'m also exploring collapsible toggles with Piston icons, and highlighted callout boxes featuring Minecraft icons, drawing inspiration from existing assets. I\'m also planning the implementation of a crafting grid table, auto-generated table of contents, and a playable Minecraft Music Disc block. Furthermore, I\'m working on background dye color pickers for blocks and duplicate/move buttons. I am making use of the Web Audio API for an audio generator.\n\n\n"
  }
}
