    thinking: "**Considering Initial Character Options**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the initial character options for CraftDocs. My current thought is to allow users to select from a character avatar, like Steve or Alex, during the signup or onboarding process. This selection will personalize the initial experience for the new user, and will establish the foundation for deeper levels of personalization to follow.\n\n\n**Developing Animated Companion Features**\n\nI\'m now diving into the animated companion features. I envision a pixelated, animated Steve or Alex character subtly peeking from the bottom right, similar to Minecraft. This interactive companion will provide tutorials, a day/night mode toggle, Minecraft references, and even a \"Spawn Creeper\" feature for playful page destruction! I\'m planning to save the character profile in state/localStorage.\n\n\n**Expanding Feature Set Design**\n\nI\'m now deeply engaged in expanding CraftDocs\' feature set, drawing inspiration from both Google Docs and Notion. I\'m focusing on incorporating clear tooltips, labels, and visible tool categories. I\'m prioritizing rich features such as diverse text formatting, background highlights, and varied text alignment options. I\'m also planning to create specific block types inspired by Minecraft, such as a crafting table grid for tables, and custom icons for callout blocks. I\'m aiming for Minecraft-themed checkmarks for to-do lists, and incorporating code blocks and video embeds. I need to update `src/types/editor.ts`.\n\n\n"
