  planner_response {
    response: "I have updated **CraftDocs** with the requested character onboarding, animated companion assistant, and Google Docs & Notion tools.\n\n### What Was Built & Enhanced\n\n1. **Steve & Alex Signup & Character Selection**:\n   - **Avatar Onboarding**: At signup, users choose their character avatar (**Steve** or **Alex**) and set their player username and initial world theme preference.\n   - **Persistence & Profile Settings**: Character choice is stored in local memory and can be changed anytime from the top hotbar header.\n\n2. **Steve / Alex Animated Companion Helper (Peeking Bottom Right)**:\n   - **Corner Peeking Animation**: Steve or Alex peeks out from the bottom-right corner of the canvas with pixelated idle bobbing and waving animations.\n   - **Interactive AI Helper Menu**: Clicking the companion opens a speech bubble with:\n     - \360\237\216\223 **Interactive Guided Tour**: A step-by-step guide explaining Survival Mode (Google Docs style continuous page) vs. Creative Mode (Notion block drag & drop), slash commands, and inventory sidebar navigation.\n     - \342\230\200\357\270\217 / \360\237\214\231 **Day vs. Night Mode Switcher**: Toggles between Overworld Light Parchment and Dark Nether Obsidian themes.\n     - \360\237\222\241 **Minecraft Tip Generator**: Provides documentation shortcuts and Minecraft lore references.\n     - \360\237\222\243 **Spawn Creeper (Detonate Page)**: Triggers an animated Creeper that walks out, flashes white and green with a \"Sssssss...\" fuse effect, screen shake, TNT explosion particles, and clears the page content.\n\n3. **Expanded Google Docs & Notion Tooling**:\n   - **Visible Hotbar Toolbar**: Clear tool labels, tooltips, and category dividers.\n   - **Google Docs Formatting**: Text formatting (Bold, Italic, Underline, Strikethrough, Subscript, Superscript), Text Alignment (Left, Center, Right, Justify), Minecraft Dye Text Color Picker (Redstone Red, Gold Yellow, Emerald Green, Diamond Cyan, Lapis Blue, Netherite Dark), Text Highlight Palette, and Undo/Redo history buttons.\n   - **Notion Block Features**: To-Do Checklists with Minecraft checkmarks (`/todo`), Expandable Accordion Toggles (`/toggle`), Minecraft Callout Boxes with custom mob/item icons (`/callout`), 3x3 Crafting Table Grid editor (`/table`), Redstone Code Blocks (`/code`), and Drag & Drop block handles."
    thinking: "**Reviewing User Requests**\n\nI\'m pleased to report that the `compile_applet` and `lint_applet` stages completed successfully. Now, I\'m carefully reviewing everything built to make sure all user requests are fully met. I\'m focusing on the character choice at signup: the `SignupModal` allows users to pick between Steve (Classic Hero) and Alex (Explorer) during the signup flow. I\'m also ensuring the user entry fields work as intended.\n\n\n**Adding User Profile Features**\n\nI\'ve been working on integrating username persistence and world theme selection using `loadUserProfile` and `saveUserProfile`, which can also be reopened via the toolbar. Now, the `MinecraftCompanion` component is rendering in the bottom right, displaying Steve or Alex pixel avatars. There\'s also an interactive dialog with a tutorial, theme toggle (Overworld Day vs Nether Night), a tip generator, and a \"Spawn Creeper\" option.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I have updated **CraftDocs** with the requested character onboarding, animated companion assistant, and Google Docs & Notion tools.\n\n### What Was Built & Enhanced\n\n1. **Steve & Alex Signup & Character Selection**:\n   - **Avatar Onboarding**: At signup, users choose their character avatar (**Steve** or **Alex**) and set their player username and initial world theme preference.\n   - **Persistence & Profile Settings**: Character choice is stored in local memory and can be changed anytime from the top hotbar header.\n\n2. **Steve / Alex Animated Companion Helper (Peeking Bottom Right)**:\n   - **Corner Peeking Animation**: Steve or Alex peeks out from the bottom-right corner of the canvas with pixelated idle bobbing and waving animations.\n   - **Interactive AI Helper Menu**: Clicking the companion opens a speech bubble with:\n     - \360\237\216\223 **Interactive Guided Tour**: A step-by-step guide explaining Survival Mode (Google Docs style continuous page) vs. Creative Mode (Notion block drag & drop), slash commands, and inventory sidebar navigation.\n     - \342\230\200\357\270\217 / \360\237\214\231 **Day vs. Night Mode Switcher**: Toggles between Overworld Light Parchment and Dark Nether Obsidian themes.\n     - \360\237\222\241 **Minecraft Tip Generator**: Provides documentation shortcuts and Minecraft lore references.\n     - \360\237\222\243 **Spawn Creeper (Detonate Page)**: Triggers an animated Creeper that walks out, flashes white and green with a \"Sssssss...\" fuse effect, screen shake, TNT explosion particles, and clears the page content.\n\n3. **Expanded Google Docs & Notion Tooling**:\n   - **Visible Hotbar Toolbar**: Clear tool labels, tooltips, and category dividers.\n   - **Google Docs Formatting**: Text formatting (Bold, Italic, Underline, Strikethrough, Subscript, Superscript), Text Alignment (Left, Center, Right, Justify), Minecraft Dye Text Color Picker (Redstone Red, Gold Yellow, Emerald Green, Diamond Cyan, Lapis Blue, Netherite Dark), Text Highlight Palette, and Undo/Redo history buttons.\n   - **Notion Block Features**: To-Do Checklists with Minecraft checkmarks (`/todo`), Expandable Accordion Toggles (`/toggle`), Minecraft Callout Boxes with custom mob/item icons (`/callout`), 3x3 Crafting Table Grid editor (`/table`), Redstone Code Blocks (`/code`), and Drag & Drop block handles."
