  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Missing Features**\n\nI\'m currently focused on identifying the missing features to bring this Minecraft-themed editor closer to the experience of Google Docs. The immediate point of consideration is establishing A4 as the default page size, addressing the user\'s specific mandates regarding page formatting, to ensure the document behaves more like standard word processor output.\n\n\n**Specifying Page Dimensions**\n\nI\'ve been drilling down into the specific page dimensions and visual characteristics. I\'ve standardized the A4 size, and incorporated scalable responsive CSS. Now, I\'m thinking about a clean white default page color with a subtle border and options including US Letter, Legal, and Minecraft Book. Further, I\'m defining orientation, margins, and background colors with a page setup dialog.\n\n\n**Enumerating Core Features**\n\nI\'m now cataloging essential Google Docs features to implement within the Minecraft theme. I\'m focusing on the top menu bar, breaking down each section: File, Edit, View, Insert, and Format. The goal is to identify and list all necessary features within each, aiming for a direct analog to Google Docs functionality. Specifically, the \"File\" menu is very important, with options like \"Page Setup\" key.\n\n\n**Detailing Formatting Options**\n\nI\'m now detailing all the formatting controls I need to incorporate. This includes text styles: bold, italic, underline, etc., and paragraph styles like headings, along with alignment, line spacing, and a \"clear formatting\" option. I\'m also considering useful tools such as word count, spell check, and a fun \"detonate page\" feature. I\'m planning to add a help section with keyboard shortcuts, a tutorial, and \"About CraftDocs\".\n\nI\'m also specifying the Google Docs horizontal ruler: I\'m picturing it styled with pixelated markings and margin indicators, along with a crisp, high-contrast, beautiful white A4 page container, realistic document shadow and padding. I\'ve designed a page numbering indicator and multi-page/visual page break support.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 4
      nanos: 777859038
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
