    thinking: "**Analyzing the Prompt\'s Intent**\n\nOkay, I\'m focusing intently on the prompt. I\'ve parsed the initial request for page size options, noting the crucial need for A4 as the default white page. My next step is to address the identified UI bugs and errors for improved functionality and a more user-friendly interface. I\'m exploring enhancements beyond the core functionality to achieve a default document editor appearance.\n\n\n**Deconstructing the Existing UI**\n\nI\'m now diving deep into Google Docs\' UI and feature set. I\'ve begun to break down its structure into the header and menu bar components. Currently, I\'m mapping out the key features like document title, save status, share buttons, and the various dropdown menus under File, Edit, View, Insert, and Format. My next goal is to translate these features into a Minecraft-themed analog.\n\n\n**Mapping Feature Analogues**\n\nI\'m now making steady progress on translating Google Docs\' formatting and insert features. I\'ve successfully mapped actions like undo/redo, print, and spell check. I\'m also working on creating pixelated analogs for zoom, text styles, font families, and font sizes. Formatting options like bold, italic, underline, text, and highlight colors are next on my list to complete!\n\n\n**Defining Formatting Options**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on defining text alignment and line spacing. I\'ve considered options like right, left, and justify alignment. Furthermore, I\'ve set up different line spacing options, like 1.0, 1.15, 1.5, and 2.0. I\'m also including list options, structure tools, and a button to set the page size with the A4. Next, I am incorporating a clear formatting tool.\n\n**Configuring Document Layout**\n\nNow I\'m focusing on defining the document stage layout. I\'m building out a classic Google Docs style horizontal ruler with margin and indent markers. The paper itself is centered against a subtle background. I\'m setting the default paper as pure white and A4 size. I\'m also addressing clean document margins.\n\n\n**Implementing Page Options**\n\nI\'m now deep-diving into the visual aspects, focusing on page presentation options. I\'m exploring page shadows and break indicators for multiple pages. Also, I\'m defining the range of page sizes and colors, including the default A4 and white. The Page Setup modal is nearly complete, and I am configuring the paper color palette and orientation settings.\n\n\n"
