  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Examining Page Styles**\n\nOkay, I\'m currently looking into how page styles are handled within `CreativeEditor.tsx` and `SurvivalEditor.tsx`. I\'ve noticed hardcoded background classes like `mc-parchment-bg` and `mc-night-parchment`, along with text colors. This suggests a rigid approach. I will now examine how these are applied as the page size and options change.\n\n\n**Defining Page Configurations**\n\nI\'m now creating comprehensive types and models, specifically `PageSize`, `PageOrientation`, `PageColor`, and `MarginOption` within `src/types/editor.ts`. I have established a `PageSettings` interface to bundle these. The default values include an A4 white portrait with normal margins. The aim is to move toward a more dynamic approach that accommodates varied configurations. I\'m also planning to incorporate more Google Docs-esque features.\n\n\n**Calculating Page Dimensions**\n\nI\'ve transitioned to defining page dimensions and margins. I\'ve calculated CSS dimensions for various page sizes, including A4, Letter, Legal, Book & Quill, Tabloid, and a fluid pageless option. I am currently integrating the margin styles to accommodate a normal, narrow, and wide setting. I aim for this to provide precise styling to meet varying user needs and allow a robust editing workflow.\n\n\n**Defining Page Appearance**\n\nI am now outlining page color themes. I\'ve defined styles for white (the default), parchment, ivory, obsidian, and void, encompassing background colors, text colors, and borders. These aim to provide a diverse range of page appearances. Next, I plan to work on horizontal rulers.\n\n\n**Designing Menu Bar**\n\nI am now focusing on the implementation of a Google Docs-style menu bar in `src/components/GoogleDocsMenuBar.tsx`. I\'ve outlined the top row including the document title, star toggle, cloud sync status, share/export, settings, and mode toggle. The bottom row will house the menu items: File, Edit, View, Insert, Format, Tools, and Help with dropdowns. I\'ve begun to define the items under File, including new document, export formats like PDF, plain text, markdown and HTML, page setup, and print options, and including the relevant keyboard shortcuts.\n\n\n**Expanding Menu Structure**\n\nI\'m now detailing the \"Edit\", \"View\", \"Insert\", and \"Format\" menu options for the Google Docs-style menu bar. Under \"Edit,\" I\'ve added \"Copy\", \"Paste\", \"Select All\", \"Find and replace\", and \"Clear formatting,\" including relevant keyboard shortcuts. \"View\" now incorporates mode toggling (Survival and Creative), ruler visibility, sidebar visibility, zoom levels, and a full-screen toggle. \"Insert\" will have image insertion (with URL and Minecraft preset options), table insertion (with an interactive grid), horizontal lines, special characters and Minecraft glyphs, page breaks, links, date/timestamp insertion. \"Format\" will feature text styling (bold, italics, etc.), paragraph styles (title, headings, etc.), and alignment/indentation options.\n\n\n**Adding Menu & Toolbar**\n\nI\'ve just added \"Tools\" and \"Help\" menu options, including keyboard shortcuts, and interactive tutorials. I am moving on to designing the Google Docs-style action toolbar in `src/components/Toolbar.tsx`. I am planning a comprehensive layout with clear icons and labels, including undo/redo, print, spell check, zoom selector, font options, and text/highlight colors, along with quick insert options. I am also planning clear line spacing options.\n\n\n**Implementing Modal Elements**\n\nI\'m now focusing on designing and integrating modals and dialogs. I\'ve started with a `PageSetupModal.tsx`, and I\'m adding options for page size, orientation, color, and margins. I\'m also including \"Save as Default\", \"OK\", and \"Cancel\" buttons. Then I am planning a find/replace modal, a word count modal, and a special characters modal. Finally, a table insertion modal will use a visual grid picker to allow insertion up to 6x6.\n\n**Refining Export & Print Support**\n\nI\'ve just moved on to export and printing functionality and I\'m working to make sure that the PDF exports and print output are perfect. I\'m focusing on the `@media print` rules in CSS. This is to ensure a clean, full-page A4 document without any extraneous elements like sidebars or toolbars. I am working to ensure edge-to-edge printing with no added margins.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 8
      nanos: 370788948
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
