  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Authentication Requirements**\n\nI\'m currently focused on defining the authentication components. I need to figure out how to integrate Google sign-in and allow for custom Minecraft player profiles (Steve, Alex, or user-defined). The top-right of the UI will show sign-in status, so I\'ll design that part.\n\n\n**Designing UI Integration**\n\nI\'ve been working on the UI integration, focusing on the visual elements. I\'m imagining a dropdown menu with user profile details, Google Drive link status, and character switcher. I\'m also thinking of a sign-in modal, allowing Google sign-in or custom account creation. This will persist securely and sync across pages. I also need to make sure the custom Minecraft skin avatar is available on both the Editor and Home Page.\n\n\n**Visualizing Title Screen**\n\nI\'m now diving into the Minecraft Home Page design, envisioning a stunning title screen. I\'m focusing on a dynamic 3D Minecraft panorama with animated elements, including voxel clouds and a day/night cycle. I\'m imagining a shimmering \"CRAFTDOCS\" logo with dynamic splash text. I\'m also planning the navigation bar with a search bar, view mode switcher, filter tabs, and sorting options.\n\n\n**Developing Home Page Elements**\n\nI\'m now implementing the Home Page visual details. The focus is now on the profile button and sign-in status, incorporating a character avatar. I\'m thinking about a template carousel with several document examples. I\'m also sketching out document cards with preview thumbnails, title, metadata, and interactive dropdown options. Finally, I am including a bottom action bar with status info.\n\nI\'ve also started working on the \"Realm Share / Enchanted Link\" Modal, making it accessible from different parts of the UI. It will include the document title and a share link with one-click copy and visual feedback, as well as access permissions.\n\n\n**Defining Permissions Options**\n\nI\'m now outlining permissions and sharing functionalities. I\'m focusing on defining different access modes: Adventure, Villager, and Creative, each with specific viewing and editing permissions. I\'m also considering player-specific sharing via email or gamertag, public link toggles, Google Drive sync options, and export features with QR code previews.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 10
      nanos: 199109198
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
