  planner_response {
    response: "I have updated the toolbar, menu bar, and sidebar to maximize screen space for the document:\n\n- **Compact UI Mode**:\n  - **Streamlined Toolbar**: Consolidated all essential formatting tools into a slim, single-row strip with 24\342\200\22326px buttons, compact dropdown selectors (Zoom, Style, Font, Font Size stepper), and browser tooltips (`title=\"Undo\"`, etc.), eliminating bulky stacked labels and wasted vertical space.\n  - **Compact Header Bar**: Inlined the File, Edit, View, Insert, Format, and Tools dropdowns directly into the top bar alongside document metadata, reclaiming over 100px of vertical space for the document parchment.\n  - **Quick Density Switcher**: Added an instant switcher in both the menu bar and toolbar with three modes:\n    - `\342\232\241 COMPACT`: Slim, single-row menus and toolbars tailored for maximum document focus.\n    - `\360\237\223\220 STANDARD`: Classic multi-tier Google Docs layout.\n    - `\360\237\221\201\357\270\217 ZEN`: Distraction-free full canvas mode that hides all toolbars and surfaces a minimalist floating title bar.\n\n- **Mini Rail & Compact Sidebar**:\n  - **Mini Icon Rail (~44px)**: Default compact mode displaying notes as a vertical icon rail with tooltips, quick `+` creation, and flyout search.\n  - **Full Drawer (`Expanded`)**: Accessible with 1 click (`[ \342\227\200 Rail ]` / `[ \342\226\266 Expand ]`) for the complete page hierarchy tree.\n  - **Fully Collapsible (`Hidden`)**: Hides the sidebar completely for full-width editing with an edge handle to open anytime.\n\n- **Document Canvas Optimization**:\n  - Reduced outer viewport padding to give the A4 parchment document prominence on all screen sizes."
