  planner_response {
    response: "To publish **CraftDocs** to your GitHub repository and host it on **GitHub Pages**, follow these steps:\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Export or Download Your Codebase\nYou can export your project files using the **Settings Menu** in Google AI Studio:\n- Click the **Settings** / **Export** menu in the top navigation and select **Export as ZIP** or **Push to GitHub**.\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Push to Your GitHub Repository\nOpen your terminal in your local project folder and run:\n\n```bash\n# 1. Initialize git (if not already initialized)\ngit init\ngit branch -M main\n\n# 2. Add remote repository\ngit remote add origin https://github.com/avanishkasar/CraftDocs.git\n\n# 3. Stage and commit all files\ngit add .\ngit commit -m \"feat: complete CraftDocs dual-paradigm editor with Minecraft UI\"\n\n# 4. Push to main branch\ngit push -u origin main --force\n```\n\n---\n\n### Step 3: Deploy to GitHub Pages\n\n#### Option A: Using GitHub Actions (Recommended & Automated)\n1. In your GitHub repository, navigate to **Settings** > **Pages**.\n2. Under **Build and deployment** > **Source**, select **GitHub Actions**.\n3. Create `.github/workflows/deploy.yml` in your repository:\n\n```yaml\nname: Deploy to GitHub Pages\n\non:\n  push:\n    branches: [main]\n\npermissions:\n  contents: read\n  pages: write\n  id-token: write\n\nconcurrency:\n  group: \"pages\"\n  cancel-in-progress: true\n\njobs:\n  deploy:\n    environment:\n      name: github-pages\n      url: ${{ steps.deployment.outputs.page_url }}\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    steps:\n      - name: Checkout\n        uses: actions/checkout@v4\n\n      - name: Set up Node.js\n        uses: actions/setup-node@v4\n        with:\n          node-version: 20\n          cache: \'npm\'\n\n      - name: Install dependencies\n        run: npm ci\n\n      - name: Build\n        run: npm run build\n\n      - name: Setup Pages\n        uses: actions/configure-pages@v4\n\n      - name: Upload artifact\n        uses: actions/upload-pages-artifact@v3\n        with:\n          path: \'./dist\'\n\n      - name: Deploy to GitHub Pages\n        id: deployment\n        uses: actions/deploy-pages@v4\n```\n\n#### Option B: Using `gh-pages` CLI\n```bash\nnpm install --save-dev gh-pages\n```\nAdd to `package.json` scripts:\n```json\n\"predeploy\": \"npm run build\",\n\"deploy\": \"gh-pages -d dist\"\n```\nThen run:\n```bash\nnpm run deploy\n```\n\n---\n\n### Summary of Polish & Documentation Prepared\n- **Comprehensive `README.md`**: Outlined full feature specifications (Survival WYSIWYG vs. Creative Blocks, Gemini AI spellchecker, export formats, UI density modes, and setup instructions).\n- **Clean Production Build**: Verified with zero compilation or TypeScript type errors ready for GitHub Pages hosting."
    modified_response: "To publish **CraftDocs** to your GitHub repository and host it on **GitHub Pages**, follow these steps:\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Export or Download Your Codebase\nYou can export your project files using the **Settings Menu** in Google AI Studio:\n- Click the **Settings** / **Export** menu in the top navigation and select **Export as ZIP** or **Push to GitHub**.\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Push to Your GitHub Repository\nOpen your terminal in your local project folder and run:\n\n```bash\n# 1. Initialize git (if not already initialized)\ngit init\ngit branch -M main\n\n# 2. Add remote repository\ngit remote add origin https://github.com/avanishkasar/CraftDocs.git\n\n# 3. Stage and commit all files\ngit add .\ngit commit -m \"feat: complete CraftDocs dual-paradigm editor with Minecraft UI\"\n\n# 4. Push to main branch\ngit push -u origin main --force\n```\n\n---\n\n### Step 3: Deploy to GitHub Pages\n\n#### Option A: Using GitHub Actions (Recommended & Automated)\n1. In your GitHub repository, navigate to **Settings** > **Pages**.\n2. Under **Build and deployment** > **Source**, select **GitHub Actions**.\n3. Create `.github/workflows/deploy.yml` in your repository:\n\n```yaml\nname: Deploy to GitHub Pages\n\non:\n  push:\n    branches: [main]\n\npermissions:\n  contents: read\n  pages: write\n  id-token: write\n\nconcurrency:\n  group: \"pages\"\n  cancel-in-progress: true\n\njobs:\n  deploy:\n    environment:\n      name: github-pages\n      url: ${{ steps.deployment.outputs.page_url }}\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    steps:\n      - name: Checkout\n        uses: actions/checkout@v4\n\n      - name: Set up Node.js\n        uses: actions/setup-node@v4\n        with:\n          node-version: 20\n          cache: \'npm\'\n\n      - name: Install dependencies\n        run: npm ci\n\n      - name: Build\n        run: npm run build\n\n      - name: Setup Pages\n        uses: actions/configure-pages@v4\n\n      - name: Upload artifact\n        uses: actions/upload-pages-artifact@v3\n        with:\n          path: \'./dist\'\n\n      - name: Deploy to GitHub Pages\n        id: deployment\n        uses: actions/deploy-pages@v4\n```\n\n#### Option B: Using `gh-pages` CLI\n```bash\nnpm install --save-dev gh-pages\n```\nAdd to `package.json` scripts:\n```json\n\"predeploy\": \"npm run build\",\n\"deploy\": \"gh-pages -d dist\"\n```\nThen run:\n```bash\nnpm run deploy\n```\n\n---\n\n### Summary of Polish & Documentation Prepared\n- **Comprehensive `README.md`**: Outlined full feature specifications (Survival WYSIWYG vs. Creative Blocks, Gemini AI spellchecker, export formats, UI density modes, and setup instructions).\n- **Clean Production Build**: Verified with zero compilation or TypeScript type errors ready for GitHub Pages hosting."
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
